steps:
  - text: |
      {[ht,$start]&thinsp;Open EM&bull;Scope}

      The previous tour examined energy consumption by way of **Joulescope Viewer** screenshots of raw power captures.

      We’ll now explore the _same_ captures with **EM&bull;Scope**, en&shy;abling more systematic measurement and comparison.

      While you'll continue &ldquo;watching screenshots&rdquo;, we encour&shy;age you to explore **EM&bull;Scope** at each stop.

      To that end, click **Open EM&bull;Scope** on the **EM&bull;Home** page and keep its tab handy as you advance through the tour.

      <div class="em-info">

      You should also follow the link to **Download Joulescope Viewer** in preparation for what follows.

      </div>

  - cmds:
      - view 1
    text: |
      {[ht,checklist]&thinsp;Explore the Captures}

      When initially launched, **EM&bull;Scope** displays a pre-popu&shy;lated list of _captures_ found in its default home folder {[dc,1]}&thinsp;.

      <div class="em-info">

      Buttons to the right enable you to select other capture folders, as well as to operate on the current captures.

      </div>

      Each row in the table (sorted here by **Capture** {[dc,2]} name) shows measurements and scores computed for this entry.

      Besides its familiar **Sleep&thinsp;&mu;A** and **Event&thinsp;&mu;J** measurements, each capture entry receives a pair of **EM&bull;eralds** {[dc,3]} scores.

      Before explaining **EM&bull;eralds**, let's click the last icon {[dc,4]} on the `nrf52` entry to view this capture's waveform&thinsp;&hellip;

  - cmds:
      - view 2
    text: |
      {[ht,monitor_heart]&thinsp;Inspect the Waveform}

      **Joulescope Viewer** opens in its own window, letting you inspect the capture waveform in greater detail:

      {[DC,1]} this panel gives a navigable view of all capture events<br>
      {[DC,2]} this marker shows statistics for the bracketed event<br>
      {[DC,3]} right-click on the marker to zoom into this event<br>
      {[DC,4]} right-click on the vertical axis to adjust its scale<br>
      {[DC,5]} these controls create additional markers<br>

      <div class="em-info">

      Refer to the [Joulescope Docs](https://docs.joulescope.com/en/software/joulescope_ui/widgets/waveform.html) for more information on the **Waveform** widget.

      </div>

      Against this vast trove of data shown by the **Joulescope Viewer**, we'll now pivot to a _single_ metric of efficiency&thinsp;&hellip;

  - cmds:
      - view 3
    text: |
      {[ht,electric_bolt]&thinsp;EM&bull;eralds}

      **EM&bull;eralds** combine _event energy_ and _sleep power_ into a single gamified score for a chosen repetition period:

      <div style="margin: 0.5em 3em;">
        <span style="text-align: center; display: inline-block; border: 1px solid #4ec9b0;
                     border-radius: 8px; padding: 0.4em 0.7em;">
          <b>EM&bull;eralds = 80 &divide; J/day</b>
        </span>
        &ensp;<a href="https://novelbits.io/bluejoule/#emeralds">&ensp;Why 80&thinsp;??&nbsp;</a>
      </div>      

      For the _fixed_ workload period {[dc,1]}, **EM&bull;Scope** calculates daily energy consumption from other raw measurements.

      For _projected_ (longer) workload periods {[dc,2]}-{[dc,4]}, **EM&bull;Scope** extrapolates `J/day` from these same measurements.

      <div class="em-info">

      Click the stopwatch icon to choose another period &ndash; and
      note how SLEEP dominates as these periods grow.

      </div>

      Since higher ≡ better, **EM&bull;eralds** scores intuitively reward econom&shy;ical WORK in combination with frugal SLEEP.

  - cmds:
      - view 4
    text: |
      {[ht,timeline]&thinsp;Rescan a Capture}

      Starting with raw power signals, **EM&bull;Scope** can _scan_ this data to locate meaningful segments of WORK and SLEEP.

      <div class="em-info">

      A later tour shows how to _grab_ a raw power capture.

      </div>

      To illustrate, let's change the _event window_ from 20&thinsp;ms to 100&thinsp;ms, and then update the table by re-scanning:

      {[DC,1]} click the gear icon, which displays current settings <br>
      {[DC,2]} update the event window duration accordingly <br>
      {[DC,3]} save your changes to the capture folder settings<br>
      {[DC,4]} click the refresh icon to rescan the capture folder<br>
      {[DC,5]} note the update to the event window duration<br>
      {[DC,6]} inspect changes in measurements and scores<br>

      The longer window slightly changes WORK and SLEEP meas&shy;urements, as well as _projected_ **EM&bull;eralds** scores.

  - cmds:
      - view 5
    text: |
      {[ht,$extra]&thinsp;Extra Credit}

      {[bi,task_alt]} TODO

      {[bi,task_alt]} TOD

      {[bi,task_alt]} TODO

  - cmds:
      - open 6
    text: |
      {[ht,$steps]&thinsp;Next Steps}

      {[hc]}
